{
  "title": "Replace hand-rolled CurrentVersionRow tuples in recipe handlers \
with RecipeVersion selects",
  "description": "update.rs, normalize_title.rs, generate_description.rs, and \
generate_photo.rs in server/src/api/recipes/ each define a near-identical \
16-field `type CurrentVersionRow = (...)` tuple (with \
#[allow(clippy::type_complexity)]) plus a 16-way destructure, purely to read \
the current version's fields. crate::models::RecipeVersion already models this \
row and diesel's `RecipeVersion::as_select()` can be selected in a tuple \
alongside the needed recipes columns (the pipeline steps in \
server/src/scraping/steps.rs already read whole RecipeVersion structs this \
way).\n\
\n\
Converting the handlers would delete the four tuple aliases and destructures, \
and would let them build their new versions via NewRecipeVersion::copy_of \
(added in the recipe-version write service PR) instead of hand-copying every \
field, so a new recipe_versions column can't be silently dropped by one \
handler. Behavior-preserving; server-only; no client changes; no `make \
pipeline` data/ diffs expected.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "api",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-07-02T13:25:00-07:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-07-02T13:25:00-07:00",
}
